From 6538d25eab52ae4cdb8cd3748b209cd4830e1f16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neiro fix <engineer@curialy.local>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:11:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(glass): capped glass renders live unless the host
 opts in to the off-screen renderer

A 120 Hz Android 16 / Mali phone (realme RMX3563, Dimensity 8100) is
auto-classified Balanced, cap 60, so every glass surface ran through
GlassFrameCache's second HardwareRenderer. The sample then died four times
in 25 s with SIGSEGV on RenderThread (fault addresses 0x38, 0x3f800038 and
float/ASCII data: a use-after-free) when a page scrolled or a control was
tapped. Rendering capped glass off screen is now opt-in
(GlasmioPerformanceConfig.cachedGlass, GlasmioPerformance.cachedGlass);
without it frameRateCap gates the glass clocks only, as in 0.2.1.
GlassFrameCacheOptInTest, GlasmioPerformanceTest.cachedGlassIsOptIn.
